  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Same time, same message",
      "items": [
        "An unknown username still runs the PBKDF2 comparison, against a real hash of a random string",
        "Unknown user and wrong password throw the identical ApiError text",
        "Passwords.verify compares in constant time with MessageDigest.isEqual"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Why the token is not stateless",
      "items": [
        "The JWT carries a session id, and every authenticated request re-reads the sessions row",
        "Sign-out deletes that row, so the token dies immediately instead of at its 60-minute expiry",
        "That costs one database read per request, which is the deliberate price"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Open before real use",
      "items": [
        "returnCodeToCaller is true, so the registration OTP is printed to stdout and returned in the response body",
        "The access token is stored in plaintext SharedPreferences",
        "PBKDF2 is a reasonable choice needing no new dependency, not the current OWASP first recommendation"
      ]
    }
  ]
